44. Tim sort - Insertion sort + Merge sort
    How it Works:
    1. Divide the array into small segments called "runs" (typically 32 or 64 elements).
    2. Sort each run using insertion sort (efficient for small datasets).
    3. Merge the sorted runs using a merge process similar to merge sort.

    Note - Insertion Sort is very efficient for small arrays (better than quicksort/merge sort in practice when n is upto 64).
    For an array of size 20, Insertion Sort is the most efficient choice.

